  "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=\u27e83{e}^{t-5},\\,\\sqrt{t+4},\\,(t-3)^{4}\u27e9$ at $t=5?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=5$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =\u27e83{e}^{5-5},\\sqrt{5+4},(5-3)^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{e}^{0},\\sqrt{9},{2}^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,3,16\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=5$ is the vector $\u27e83,3,16\u27e9.$",
